            <ArticleTitle>Role of polymers in improving the results of stenting in coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>685-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article is a review of recent developments of polymer-related stents mainly employed in the coronary arteries, including polymer-coated stents, biostable stents and biodegradable stents. Polymer paving is covered as well. The problems with the stents currently investigated and the development of new stents are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
